{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"automorphismGroup","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17IsomorphismModule17AutomorphismGroupV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/AutomorphismGroup","text":"AutomorphismGroup","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Found by individualization–refinement with automorphism pruning (McKay & Piperno 2014;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Junttila & Kaski 2007): the search tree of one graph, each later leaf compared with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first, the branches an automorphism found so far maps onto a searched one skipped. Runs to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completion (it does not check for task cancellation). Exponential in the worst case (as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nauty and bliss); near-linear refinement per search node, and on most graphs a few nodes per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"base vertex.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automorphism group: the permutations of the vertices that keep the number of edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between every pair of vertices (self-loops included), with generators, orbits and order."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/automorphismGroup()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocol